:Namespace ClassicNames
⍝ Non-ASCII file names in Classic interpreters on non-Windows platforms.
⍝ Classic writes such names as one ANSI byte per character (⎕ → 0x8C), while Unicode
⍝ interpreters write UTF-8. Link translates names so that Classic writes UTF-8 too.
⍝ Wildcard ⎕NINFO lists names in filesystem form (v22 and later).
⍝ "Filesystem form" is a character vector whose ⎕NXLATE bytes are the bytes on disk;
⍝ every ⎕N function accepts it unchanged. Elsewhere all functions defer to the primitives.
⍝ Everything here runs at ⎕FIX time without ##.U

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1
    Affected←(82=⎕DR'')∧'Windows'≢7↑⊃'.'⎕WG'APLVersion'

    ∇ r←ToFS name;b;a
    ⍝ Name → filesystem form (UTF-8 on disk, as written by Unicode interpreters)
      →0⍴⍨~Affected⊣r←name
      b←'UTF-8'⎕UCS name
      r←⎕AV[(⎕NXLATE 0)⍳b] ⋄ a←⍸b<128 ⋄ r[a]←⎕UCS b[a]
    ∇

    ∇ r←FromFS name;b;a
    ⍝ Filesystem form → name. Names that are not valid UTF-8 (written by Classic
    ⍝ without ToFS) are already in ⎕AV characters and are returned unchanged.
      →0⍴⍨~Affected⊣r←name
      b←(⎕NXLATE 0)[⎕AV⍳name] ⋄ a←⍸name∊⎕UCS 31+⍳95 ⋄ b[a]←⎕UCS name[a]
      :Trap 0 ⋄ r←'UTF-8'⎕UCS b ⋄ :EndTrap
    ∇

:EndNamespace
